{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7f4c1a2-9d3e-4f61-8c2a-1e5d7a9b3c40",
    "name": "Vouch — verify every claim",
    "description": "Every public claim Vouch makes, as a request you can run yourself.\n\nA registry whose argument is that unverified claims are worthless should not ask you to take its README on trust. So this collection reads the deployed contracts on Creditcoin CC3 Testnet over plain JSON-RPC, and each request carries a test that asserts the exact value the documentation promises. Import it, press Run, and the claims either pass or they do not.\n\nNothing here needs a wallet, an API key, or a node. It is `eth_call` against a public RPC, which is the cheapest possible way for a stranger to check our work.\n\n## What the run proves\n\n1. The v2 registry holds a real Aave repayment proven from Sepolia through the Attestcoin Block Prover.\n2. Four independent consumers read that one fact and each grant a different benefit.\n3. An address with no proof gets the baseline from every one of them, so the benefit is coming from the proof rather than from the contract being generous.\n4. Standing does not leak between fact types: the same proof that moves collateral leaves the exchange fee untouched.\n\nThe third and fourth are the ones worth watching. A lending contract that returns a good number for everybody has not demonstrated anything.\n\n## Variables\n\n`subject` is the proven address. `control` is `0x…dEaD`, which has no facts and never will, and exists so every benefit can be read against a baseline in the same run.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "rpc",
      "value": "https://rpc.cc3-testnet.creditcoin.network",
